iolent in reaction","thermalState":"Chilly, with cold extremities and blueness during attacks","coldSensitivity":"Cold hands and feet; bluish face, lips and nails during spasms","weakness":["Sudden prostration and collapse","Great weariness of the limbs","Weak, scarcely perceptible pulse during severe attacks"],"sensitivity":["Pains increased by movement and touch"],"sidePreference":"Complaints may begin on the left side","generalTendencies":["Spasms and cramps","Cyanosis","Collapse","Periodic attacks in groups"]},"causation":["Fright","Suppressed eruptions or discharges","Anger","Over-exertion of mind","Loss of sleep"],"modalities":{"aggravation":["Before menses","From vomiting","Contact and touch","Movement","Night"],"amelioration":["Drinking cold water","During perspiration","Pressure over the heart","Stretching the affected limb (calf cramp)"]},"foodAndAppetite":{"appetite":"Intense nausea may dominate the picture","cravings":["Cold drinks"],"thirst":"Craves cool water","ameliorations":["Cold water relieves vomiting, colic, cough and spasm"]},"sleepAndDreams":{"sleep":["Suffocative attacks around 3 a.m."],"insomnia":["Loss of sleep may precipitate the complaints"]},"particulars":{"head":["Violent headache with nausea"],"face":["Pale, bluish or livid face during spasms"],"mouth":["Strong metallic, slimy taste with salivation"],"git":["Nausea greater than in most remedies","Vomiting relieved by drinking cold water","Colic with diarrhoea and cramps","Hiccough preceding the spasms","Fluid descends with a gurgling sound when drinking"],"respiratory":["Spasmodic cough with a purple face","Whooping cough better from a swallow of cold water","Suffocative attacks around 3 a.m."],"heartAndCirculation":["Palpitation with anxiety","Constriction with bluish lips and cold extremities"],"femaleGenital":["Menses too late and protracted","Cramps before, during or after suppressed menses"],"extremitiesAndJoints":["Clonic spasms beginning in the fingers and toes","Clenched thumbs","Cramps in the calves and soles","Coldness of the hands","Jerking and twitching of the muscles"],"urinary":["Suppression of urine associated with convulsions (traditional description)"],"skin":["Suppressed eruptions may be followed by vomiting, stupor or convulsions"],"nerves":["Chorea after fright","Epileptic aura beginning in the knees"]},"fever":{"chill":["Chilliness with cold, blue extremities"],"heat":["Heat of the head with cold hands during spasms"],"sweat":["Cold sweat with collapse"],"pattern":"Attacks appear periodically and in groups","associatedSymptoms":["Nausea","Cramps","Cyanosis"]},"sensations":["Cramping and contractive pain","Coldness of the extremities","Metallic taste","Constriction of the chest"],"locationAndDirection":{"location":["Fingers and toes","Calves and soles","Abdomen","Chest"],"side":"May begin on the left side","direction":["Spasms ascend from the knees","Cramps spread from the fingers and toes toward the body"]},"concomitants":["Nausea and vomiting with cramps","Cold sweat with spasms","Cyanosis with convulsions"],"pediatric":{"general":["Convulsions in children"],"behaviour":["Piercing shrieks during spasms"],"fever":["Convulsions with fever"],"digestive":["Colic with vomiting"],"characteristicSymptoms":["Clenched thumbs during convulsions","Whooping cough with a purple face and exhaustion after the paroxysm"]},"constitutionAndLifeStage":{"constitution":"Spasmodic and irritable","age":"Especially children and debilitated or prematurely aged adults","lifeStage":"During teething and childhood illnesses, and in old age with cramps","typicalPatientPicture":"A patient prone to violent cramps and spasms, with cold blue extremities, intense nausea and a marked relief from cold drinks."},"compareWith":[{"medicine":"Belladonna","similarities":["Convulsions","Sudden onset","Violent symptoms"],"differences":["Belladonna has a hot, red face and dilated pupils; Cuprum has a cold, blue or livid face","Belladonna is worse from light, noise and jarring","Cuprum spasms often begin in the fingers and toes with clenched thumbs"]},{"medicine":"Cicuta virosa","similarities":["Convulsions","Spasmodic affections"],"differences":["Cicuta features opisthotonos and marked head retraction","Cuprum is more often associated with peripheral onset and cyanosis","The Cuprum picture includes intense nausea and relief from cold water"]},{"medicine":"Veratrum album","similarities":["Cramps","Cold sweat","Collapse"],"differences":["Veratrum album has profuse watery diarrhoea and vomiting with icy coldness","Cuprum is dominated by spasms and convulsions rather than fluid loss","Cuprum has the characteristic metallic taste and cold-water amelioration"]}],"relationships":{"complementary":["Calcarea carbonica"],"antidotes":["Belladonna","Hepar sulphuris","Camphora"],"relatedRemedies":["Cuprum sulphuricum (burning at the vertex; spasmodic cough)"]},"therapeuticApplications":{"note":"The following are traditional homeopathic Materia Medica associations for educational study only. They are not evidence-based medical treatment recommendations. Convulsions, whooping cough and severe cramps require urgent medical assessment.","applications":["Traditional association with convulsions and spasms","Nocturnal cramps of the calves and soles in debilitated or elderly patients","Spasmodic cough and the whooping-cough picture","Nausea and vomiting with cramps","Complaints following suppressed eruptions"]},"quickRevision":{"keyPoints":["Violent cramps and convulsions","Begins in fingers and toes","Clenched thumbs","Blue face and cold extremities","Better from cold water"],"mind":["Unconquerable anxiety","Restless tossing","Anger preceding spasms"],"physicalGenerals":["Cyanosis","Coldness","Sudden collapse","Periodicity in groups"],"modalities":["Aggravation before menses, from touch, movement and vomiting","Amelioration from cold drinks and during perspiration"],"foodAndThirst":["Craves cold drinks","Cold water relieves vomiting and spasm"],"majorSystems":["Nervous","Muscular","Digestive","Respiratory"],"characteristicSymptoms":["Clenched thumbs during convulsions","Epileptic aura beginning in the knees","Metallic taste with salivation"]},"examFocus":{"importantConcepts":["Spasms and convulsions","Peripheral onset of cramps","Cyanosis","Cold-water amelioration","Periodicity in groups"],"frequentlyAskedTopics":["Characteristic symptoms of Cuprum metallicum","Cuprum in convulsions and cramps","Cuprum in whooping cough"],"shortNoteTopics":["Cuprum metallicum","Cuprum in spasmodic affections"],"compareQuestions":["Cuprum versus Belladonna in convulsions","Cuprum versus Veratrum album in cramps and collapse","Cuprum versus Cicuta virosa in convulsions"],"pediatricTopics":["Convulsions in children with clenched thumbs","Whooping cough with a purple face"],"characteristicSymptoms":["Cramps beginning in the fingers and toes","Aura beginning in the knees","Metallic taste with salivation"],"modalities":["Aggravation from touch, movement and before menses","Amelioration from cold water"]},"traditionalNote":"This entry organizes traditional Homeopathic Materia Medica descriptions for educational and examination-reference purposes. It should not be interpreted as evidence-based medical treatment advice. Copper is toxic in material doses; convulsions and severe cramps are medical emergencies."}$materia_medica_json$::jsonb,
