  $materia_medica_json${"id":"MED-004","slug":"cephalandra-indica","name":"Cephalandra Indica","commonName":"Ivy Gourd","scientificName":"Coccinia grandis (synonyms: Coccinia indica, Cephalandra indica)","abbreviation":"Ceph.","synonyms":["Coccinia indica","Coccinia grandis","Cephalandra indica","Ivy Gourd","Telakucha","Kundru","Scarlet-fruited Gourd"],"source":"Plant","origin":"Native to India and tropical Asia; also found in tropical Africa","naturalOrder":"Cucurbitales","family":"Cucurbitaceae (gourd family)","kingdom":"Plantae","habitat":"A climbing vine of tropical and subtropical regions, often growing wild on fences and trees","partUsed":"Fresh leaves and aerial parts; the fruit and root are also used in traditional practice","preparation":"Mother tincture prepared from the fresh plant; also used in low attenuations in traditional Indian practice","chemicalConstituents":["Cucurbitacin-type bitter principles","Resins","Enzyme principles (reported)","Sugars and mucilage"],"alkaloids":["Traces of an alkaloid reported in the plant"],"generalAnalysis":"A remedy that comes from Indian clinical practice rather than the classical provings of Boericke or Clarke. Its traditional picture is built around profuse urination with exhaustion, intense thirst, dryness of the mouth and burning sensations relieved by cold, together with recurrent boils and carbuncles. It is studied chiefly for its traditional association with the diabetic symptom picture, which must not be confused with evidence of treatment.","sphereOfAction":["Urinary system","Metabolic and endocrine system (traditional association)","Skin","Digestive system","Eyes"],"drugPicture":{"generalPicture":"A picture of fluid loss and burning: the patient passes large quantities of urine and feels exhausted afterwards, is very thirsty for large draughts of water, has a dry burning mouth and a burning sensation over the body that cold applications relieve. Boils and carbuncles may recur, and giddiness is worse after urination.","generalCharacteristics":["Profuse urination with exhaustion and weakness afterwards","Great thirst for large quantities of water at a time","Dryness of the mouth with burning","Burning sensations all over the body, better from cold","Recurrent boils, carbuncles and abscesses","Giddiness worse after urination"],"typicalConstitution":"Described in traditional Indian practice in adults with a diabetic picture of polyuria, thirst and debility","temperament":"Morose, fretful and disinclined to work","generalTendencies":["Polyuria with debility","Burning pains","Boils and slow-healing skin lesions","Biliousness and flatulent distension"],"characteristicFeatures":["Weakness and exhaustion after passing urine","Burning relieved by anything cold","Redness and burning of the face","Headache from exposure to the sun"]},"keySymptoms":{"keynotes":["Copious urination with exhaustion and weakness afterwards","Great thirst for large quantities of water at a time","Dryness of the mouth with burning","Burning all over the body, ameliorated by cold applications","Recurrent boils and carbuncles (traditional clinical association)","Giddiness worse after urination"],"guidingSymptoms":["Redness of the face with burning","Burning of the eyes","Biliousness with distension of the abdomen","Greenish mucous stools mixed or tinged with blood","Sugar in the urine (traditional clinical observation)"],"characteristicSymptoms":["Worse after urination","Amelioration from cold bathing and cold applications","Headache from exposure to the sun","Dry mouth with thirst for large draughts"],"indicatingSymptoms":["Polyuria with post-micturition exhaustion","Burning pains with redness of the face","Recurrent boils in a patient with thirst and polyuria"]},"mind":{"general":["Morose and fretful","Disinclined to do any work","Gloomy"],"sadness":["Gloomy mood with aversion to activity"]},"physicalGenerals":{"constitution":"Traditional clinical picture in adults with polyuria, thirst and debility","te