typicalPatientPicture":"A thirsty patient passing large quantities of urine, exhausted afterwards, with burning sensations and recurrent boils."},"relationships":{},"therapeuticApplications":{"note":"These are traditional homeopathic and Indian clinical associations for educational study only; they are not evidence-based treatment recommendations. Diabetes mellitus requires medical diagnosis, monitoring and treatment. Homeopathic Cephalandra must never replace prescribed diabetes care or insulin.","applications":["Traditional association with the diabetic symptom picture (polyuria, thirst, boils)","Traditional use for boils, carbuncles and abscesses","Traditional use for burning sensations over the body","Traditional use for biliousness and flatulent distension","Traditional use for headache from exposure to the sun"]},"quickRevision":{"keyPoints":["Polyuria with exhaustion","Great thirst for large draughts","Burning better from cold","Boils and carbuncles","Giddiness after urination"],"mind":["Morose","Fretful","Disinclined to work"],"physicalGenerals":["Burning sensations","Debility","Dryness"],"modalities":["Aggravation after urination and from heat","Amelioration from cold applications"],"foodAndThirst":["Loss of appetite","Intense thirst for large quantities of water"],"majorSystems":["Urinary","Skin","Digestive","Eyes"],"characteristicSymptoms":["Exhaustion after urination","Burning better from cold","Recurrent boils"]},"examFocus":{"importantConcepts":["Remedy from Indian clinical practice","Polyuria with debility","Burning ameliorated by cold","Boils and carbuncles","Traditional diabetic picture"],"frequentlyAskedTopics":["Cephalandra indica in the traditional diabetic picture","Burning sensations of Cephalandra indica","Cephalandra indica and boils"],"shortNoteTopics":["Cephalandra indica"],"characteristicSymptoms":["Weakness after urination","Burning better from cold applications","Thirst for large quantities of water"],"modalities":["Aggravation after urination and from the sun","Amelioration from cold"]},"traditionalNote":"Cephalandra indica is not a classical remedy in Boericke or Clarke; its materia medica rests largely on Indian provings and clinical reports, so no classical remedy relationships are listed. This entry is educational only and does not present homeopathy as an evidence-based treatment for diabetes or any other disease."}$materia_medica_json$::jsonb,
